  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Resilience - Cashew income and food security in Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme has agroecology at its core and will work with farmers, their communities and associations to strengthen their focus on resilience and improved production techniques that maintain soil quality. In addition to food security the programme will support the national strategy of the Cashew Institute to give farmers more influence in the cashew sector. By securing strong cooperatives the farmers can add value by assuring quality, drying, sorting and selling directly to avoid middlemen.</narrative>
  </description>
